=== PR DESCRIPTION ===
this fixes:
* 16 bit RGB and grayscale images
* 8 bit grayscale images without alpha

png_set_gray_to_rgb expands grayscale to rgb with 8 bits, so bit_depth and color_type is changed so the png_set_filler condition will be fulfilled if it's grayscale without alpha.
same idea with png_set_scale_16, but the color_type doesn't need to be changed because it's already PNG_COLOR_TYPE_RGB(_ALPHA)

the png_set_expand and png_set_expand_gray_1_2_4_to_8 checks were redundant and i removed them.

after making these changes, i tested all images from http://www.schaik.com/pngsuite/ .
all seemed to load and look fine except for the purposefully corrupt ones.
so this is probably the last fix for valid png images.

